        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0554" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg458"/>

                <head>No. 346.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 13,
                        1872</date>. (Received September 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 633.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I transmit a copy of a note which
                    I addressed to Mr. Lafragua on the 4th instant, (A,) together with a copy of the
                    letter therein alluded to from <hi rendition="#italic">Dr</hi>. A. M. Boyd, of
                    Tuxpan, Mexico, in which he complains of excessive and illegal duties levied
                    upon American colonists in that vicinity upon the importation of machinery for
                    sugar-plantations.</p>
                <p>No reply has yet been received.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d346-a1.xml" xpointer="d346-a1"/>
